# What the image build must not see.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` sweeps the whole directory into the build
# context: a node_modules built for Windows, the filled-in `.env` with every
# production secret in it, and the local `dist`. The first makes the build slow
# and can shadow the Linux modules installed inside the image; the second puts
# credentials into a build layer for no reason; the third can be stale.
node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The OpenProject initializers are built into their own image — see
# openproject/Dockerfile. They are Ruby and this image is Node.
openproject

.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*
